# Discovery output is COMMITTED, not ignored. Which ATS a firm uses changes
# about never, and at several thousand firms re-deriving it every week is the
# most expensive thing the pipeline does. Committing the answers makes it a
# one-off you refresh deliberately with ./weekly.sh --full. None of it is
# personal — it is a public list of which company uses which job board.
companies_house.csv

# State is committed encrypted instead — see .github/workflows/weekly.yml
!jobs.db.gpg

.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
